{"type":"lesson.started","request_id":"70d5e23f-ac8b-4d49-bf87-beca09b899e2","title":"A system of two linear equations as crossing lines"}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"70d5e23f-ac8b-4d49-bf87-beca09b899e2","step":{"id":"s1","script":"Each equation draws a line. A solution to both equations must lie on both lines.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Two equations, one shared point"},{"op":"axes","id":"graph","region":"right","x":{"min":-1,"max":5,"label":"x"},"y":{"min":-1,"max":6,"label":"y"}},{"op":"equation","id":"eqone","region":"A2","latex":"y=x+1"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"70d5e23f-ac8b-4d49-bf87-beca09b899e2","step":{"id":"s2","script":"The first line shows every pair satisfying y equals x plus one. The second line shows pairs satisfying y equals negative x plus five.","ops":[{"op":"curve","id":"rising","axes_id":"graph","expr":"x+1","domain":[-1,5]},{"op":"equation","id":"eqtwo","anchor":{"el":"eqone","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"y=-x+5"},{"op":"curve","id":"falling","axes_id":"graph","expr":"-x+5","domain":[-1,5]}],"checkpoint":{"question":"What does the crossing point tell us about the two equations?","expected_gist":"Its coordinates satisfy both equations."}}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"70d5e23f-ac8b-4d49-bf87-beca09b899e2","step":{"id":"s3","script":"At the crossing, both lines have the same y value. Set their expressions equal to find x equals two.","ops":[{"op":"point","id":"crossing","construct":{"kind":"intersection_of","a":"rising","b":"falling"},"label":"(2, 3)"},{"op":"equation","id":"solve","anchor":{"el":"eqtwo","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"x+1=-x+5\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad x=2"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"70d5e23f-ac8b-4d49-bf87-beca09b899e2","step":{"id":"s4","script":"Substitute x equals two into either equation: y equals three. The shared point, two comma three, is the system's unique solution.","ops":[{"op":"equation","id":"check","anchor":{"el":"solve","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"3=2+1\\qquad 3=-2+5"},{"op":"text","id":"solution","anchor":{"el":"crossing","side":"below","gap":0.08},"content":"(2, 3) satisfies both"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.done","request_id":"70d5e23f-ac8b-4d49-bf87-beca09b899e2","accepted_steps":4,"repairs":0,"dropped_steps":0,"sanitized_steps":0,"sanitized_fields":0}
